\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Coordinate covariance and its Gaussian density}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{Let #{Q} be a [positive precision parameter](fdip-0004) on a
finite real inner-product space #{(E,h)}, with inverse-precision
covariance given by \ref{fdip-000B}.
For a chosen nonorthonormal basis #{b_i}, coordinates are the functionals
#{h(b^i,\cdot)}. The dual basis satisfies #{h(b^i,b_j)=\delta_{ij}},
so the covariance array has entries #{h(b^i,Q^{-1}b^j)}; this is not the
unqualified array of the inverse operator in that basis.
The orthonormal counting basis gives the coordinate formula in
\ref{fdip-000B}, evaluated on the alternating cycle in \ref{fdip-0037}.}
\p{For formal Gaussian providers, put #{n=\dim E}, choose an
orthonormal chart #{C:E\to\mathbb R^n}, and write #{y=Cx}.
The inverse and its chart array #{S=CQ^{-1}C^{-1}} are positive definite,
with #{S^{-1}=CQC^{-1}} and #{\det S=(\det Q)^{-1}}.
The provider density is
##{\begin{aligned}
 &(2\pi)^{-n/2}(\det S)^{-1/2}
       e^{-y^TS^{-1}y/2}\\
 &\qquad=Z_Q^{-1}e^{-h(x,Qx)/2}.
\end{aligned}}
By the [canonical-volume characterization](fdip-002M) and
\ref{fdip-002L} for isometries between counting coordinate spaces,
#{C} preserves volume. The Euclidean-space coordinate wrapper preserves
volume by \leanref{OrthonormalBasis.measurePreserving_repr} and
\leanref{PiLp.volume_preserving_toLp}. After this wrapper, the chart
pushforward of #{\mu_Q} is #{\mathrm{multivariateGaussian}(0,S)} by
\leanref/tauceti{TauCeti.Probability.multivariateGaussian_eq_withDensity}.
Mathlib's
\leanref{ProbabilityTheory.covariance_eval_multivariateGaussian}
gives coordinate covariance #{S}; its positive semidefinite hypothesis
follows from positive definiteness. The parameter is the covariance array
#{S} of #{Q^{-1}}, not the precision array #{CQC^{-1}}.
The comparison also needs these density, determinant and volume
identifications; the integral proof in \ref{fdip-000B} is independent of them.}

\p{The density comparison uses
\citet{Proposition B.55, p. 505, and Theorem 8.4, p. 385}{friedli2017statistical},
with zero mean and covariance #{S} in the specified orthonormal chart.
The nonorthonormal coordinate entries follow from \ref{fdip-000B}
on the displayed dual-basis functionals.}
